  "kanji": "管",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 管\ntitle: pipe; supervise\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 竹\nradicalNumber: 118\nonyomi: [カン]\nkunyomi: [くだ]\ndistractors: [官, 答, 笑]\n---\n\n# 管 — pipe; supervise\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 竹 (no. 118) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n管 concerns pipes or tubes and also supervision or management. The concrete native noun is くだ; 管理 uses the on reading カン for overseeing something, not for a literal pipe.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See the bamboo-shaped top over 官 and imagine an official checking a row of pipes. This is an invented memory scene based on the modern components, not their historical or phonetic roles.\n\nThe canonical key is [竹](竹.md), no. 118, in its top form ⺮.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カン | on | [管理](../words/管理.md) かんり - management; control |\n| くだ | kun | [管](../words/管.md) くだ - pipe; tube |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [管](../words/管.md) くだ - pipe; tube\n- [管理](../words/管理.md) かんり - management; control\n\n## Notes\n\n- 管 かん is also a documented noun for a pipe or tube, with further wind-instrument and anatomical senses. The linked [管](../words/管.md) article specifically teaches くだ; the two records should not be merged into one freely interchangeable pronunciation rule.\n- 管理する is transitive: mark what is managed with を. Management does not by itself establish ownership; see [管理](../words/管理.md).\n- Compare [筒](筒.md), cylinder or tube, as a genuinely overlapping meaning, not a wrong quiz answer. [官](官.md) means government official; the extra bamboo-shaped top distinguishes 管.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1214200, 1577650, 2868440.\n",
